{# The payment providers, in the "third-parties" section of UiBundle's "france/privacy-policy" model, which includes it when this bundle is installed - the app stores only once one is fully set up; the payment unit names the providers the shop offers, linked to their privacy policy where its address is known, and keeps its historical id so an edit made to it on a site still applies #}
{% set policies = {'stripe': 'https://stripe.com/privacy'} %}
<h3 data-legal-id="third-parties.stripe">Payment</h3>
<div>
	Payments are processed by our payment provider{% if payment_gateways() is not empty %} ({% for slug in payment_gateways() %}{% if policies[slug] is defined %}<a href="{{ policies[slug] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ slug|capitalize }}</a>{% else %}{{ slug|capitalize }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}){% endif %}, which is PCI-DSS certified. Your card details are entered at that provider and never reach us: we only receive the payment confirmation, with the payer's email address and name. This data is processed under that provider's privacy policy.
</div>
{% if payment_in_app_stores() is not empty %}
<h3 data-legal-id="third-parties.app-stores">In-app purchases (Apple, Google)</h3>
<div>
	Purchases made in the mobile app are processed by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play), to which they are paid. We receive from them the purchase identifier, the product bought and, where applicable, its refund, linked to your account. This data is processed under <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's</a>.
</div>
{% endif %}
